/target

# Cargo.lock is intentionally tracked in this fork (upstream ignores it). Every published
# version of `core2` is yanked, and it is a non-optional transitive dependency via
# libipld -> ssi-vc, so `cargo generate-lockfile` can no longer resolve this workspace from
# scratch. A committed lock keeps CI and vendored consumers building; drop it only once the
# libipld/core2 chain is bumped.

.vscode
